    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a7f85fe2_a3e998ff",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 1111,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-09-05T16:53:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is a sad story. I originally used chipset_in_state(CHIPSET_STATE_ANY_OFF), but when set_usb_mux_with_current_data_role is called, the chipset is still transiting into S5. The chipset is in the S3S5 state which is the (CHIPSET_STATE_SOFT_OFF | CHIPSET_STATE_SUSPEND) state. chipset_in_state(CHIPSET_STATE_ANY_OFF) returns false when in the S3S5 state.\n\nMaybe there is some other way to determine we are transiting into the S5 state without the flag, but I didn\u0027t figure it out.\n\nAlso the chipset_in_state method returns the same things for both S5S3 (turning on) and S3S5 (turning off) which also makes things more difficult for this situation.",
      "parentUuid": "b1d0a590_476191a5",
      "revId": "6b736a8cb0bd4f66be53c7d034d45f62ec8c652c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
